  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - a. General FAQ\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFrequently Asked Questions\nGeneral F.A.Q.\nWhen do I find out my student ID number?\nStudents will be sent their student ID number via email. They may also find it on the application website.\nWhy can't I log in to HUFS PortalS with my exchange application ID and PW?\nYou can only log into the course registration with your new HUFS student ID (202485XXX).\nYou will see your student ID on the exchange application portal about one month before the semester starts, and right before the first round of course registration\n. We will send you an email to let you know when it is ready, along with instructions on how to find it in the\nApplication portal\n.\nHow do I log on to campus wifi?\nSeoul Campus\nOn campus, our wifi network is:\nHufs_SeoulCampus or Hufs_Global\nThere is another network, Hufs_SeoulCampus_HELP/Hufs_Global_HELP which has a guide for doing this, but it is only in Korean\nWhen you choose Hufs_SeoulCampus/Hufs_Global as your Wifi, you should get a pop up window that asks you for your username and password.\nThese are your:\nStudent ID Number (202585XXX)\nPassword-the default password is your date of birth (YYYYMMDD).\nFor iPhone: Certificate -> \"Trust\"\nFor Android: CA Certificate -> \"Do Not Validate\"; EAP -> \"TTLS\",  MAC Address Type-> \"Use Phone/Device MAC\"\nWhich airport should I fly into?\nThis depends to a small degree on what country you are coming from. For the\nvast majority of travelers\ncoming from outside of Asia or neighboring countries, you should book your flights in/out from\nIncheon International Airport (ICN)\n. From countries such as China or Japan, it's possible to book flights to Gimpo International Airport (GMP).\nWhen does the school year start (i.e., first semester) in Korea?\nThe first semester of the academic year in Korea is in Spring from March to June. The second semester runs from September to December.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
